Z||000000||Pontiatic||11-02-2001||03:49 PM||||Well i've been trying to convince my parents (mainly my mom) to let me get a fiero gt so i could work on it for a senior project. of course she gives me the usual "u need to save..blah blah blah..." anywho is it possible to put a high powered v6 in an 85 2m4?? i heard that the manual shift can't handle it. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||11-02-2001||04:15 PM||||You can put a number of V-6 engines in there.  The easiest would probably be a 3.4 pushrod engine--it's nearly a straight bolt-in swap.  Others have put almost every kind of engine imaginable in their cars.  As for the transmission, Archie uses stock ones behind his V-8 conversions.  They seem to handle the power very well unless they are abused.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
